🐢 brains.auth.set — store a claude subscription oauth token in the global keyrack

  usage: brains.auth.set [--reach <email>]

  opens an isolated browser sign-in (never your global claude), reads that
  session's oauth refresh token, and stores it as
  BRAINS_AUTH__OF__CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN cut at that account's email, in the
  global (--org @all) keyrack — so it is reachable from any repo.

    --reach <email>  only if the account cannot be asked (rare) — the
                     email is read from the token itself by default.
                     alias: --sub (the old name, superseded)

  exit codes, for a caller that reads only $?:
    0  the account was stored
    1  it broke on our side — retry may help (no private dir, keyrack write)
    2  it needs you — a dead token, a bad flag, or a sign-in you did not finish

  example: brains.auth.set
